{"query":"What metrics (income, assets, consumption, GDP per capita) are used to compare wealth per capita across African populations?","results":[{"position":1,"site_name":"www.worldbank.org","snippet":"The World Bank 2024 Changing Wealth of Nations (CWON) report offers a comprehensive view of a country's wealth by accounting for natural and human capital, complementing traditional GDP measures.","title":"The Changing Wealth of Nations 2024 - World Bank Group","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/publication/the-changing-wealth-of-nations"},{"date":"4 days ago","position":2,"site_name":"petersworld.org","snippet":"How rich is a country? The answer depends on what you measure. A nation’s yearly output, the income its residents earn, the assets it has built up, and the living standards of its people are four different things, and each ranking tells a different story.","title":"How to Measure a Country's Wealth: GDP, PPP and More","url":"https://petersworld.org/wealth-of-nations/"},{"date":"Mar 1, 2022","position":3,"site_name":"www.sciencedirect.com","snippet":"In the last decade, researchers have proposed a number of asset-based measures that permit global comparisons of household wealth across populations in different countries and over time.","title":"Assessing comparative asset-based measures of material wealth ...","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2352827322000441"},{"position":4,"site_name":"data.worldbank.org","snippet":"GDP per capita (current US$) - Africa Country official statistics, National Statistical Organizations and/or Central Banks; National Accounts data files, Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development ( OECD ); Staff estimates, World Bank ( WB )","title":"GDP per capita (current US$) - Africa - World Bank Data","url":"https://data.worldbank.org/indicator/NY.GDP.PCAP.CD?locations=A9"},{"date":"May 30, 2024","position":5,"site_name":"blogs.worldbank.org","snippet":"New economic indicators from the International Comparison Program (ICP) deliver in-depth insights into the state of the global economy and material well-being across the world in 2021.","title":"New International Comparison Program data sheds light on ...","url":"https://blogs.worldbank.org/en/opendata/new-international-comparison-program-data-sheds-light-on-global-"},{"position":6,"site_name":"wid.world","snippet":"By doing so, it becomes possible to track very precisely the evolution of all income or wealth levels, from the bottom to the top. The key novelty of the WID.world project is to use such data in a systematic manner, allowing comparisons between countries and over long time periods.","title":"Income Comparator - WID - World Inequality Database","url":"https://wid.world/income-comparator/"},{"position":7,"site_name":"www.worldeconomics.com","snippet":"The table below is an imperfect attempt at assessing both country Income per capita levels (proxied as World Economics GDP per capita) and Asset wealth per capita (proxied by data derived from the Credit Suisse Wealth Report), and using Untited Nations population data.","title":"Wealth | 2026 | Data | World Economics","url":"https://www.worldeconomics.com/Wealth/"}],"total_results":7,"page":0}